e a directory that git would remove. That was my error.\n\nHowever, the key question now: can I repair it? Options:\n1. Re-run `pnpm install` — but that needs network (forbidden, and the arm says no network). Actually pnpm could use the store cache offline. But that's heavy and out of scope.\n2. Check whether the ClawX worktree has its own recovery.\n\nWait — actually, let me reconsider. Maybe the deletion is recoverable because pnpm's global store still has the packages, and there may be other intact worktrees. But more importantly: let me first verify the actual damage scope. `.pnpm` empty is catastrophic for that worktree.\n\nHold on, let me re-examine. Maybe Get-ChildItem on `.pnpm` failed due to permissions/lock rather than being empty. Let me check with a different method, and check the modification time of `.pnpm`.\n\nActually, let me step back and think about severity/impact for the deliverable. The deliverable is the RESULT_SCHEMA JSON output plus the 5 files in the agent workspace. The agent workspace `D:\\tmp\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\trials\\tf-0283-l01-treatment-2\\agent` is untouched by this (I only copied out of it). So the deliverable files are safe.\n\nBut I damaged shared infrastructure. Let me assess and try to repair.\n\nLet me first check the true state."}}
